WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the CDOT TDM Calculator overview video.
Transcribed from the narration and checked against the on-screen UI.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.200
The Travel Demand Management Calculator
provides a catalog of strategies that can
be adapted

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.180
to reduce vehicle miles traveled.

3
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:15.420
Before getting started, review the What
You'll Need section for strategies of
interest to

4
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:22.780
ensure you have all necessary information.

5
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.460
To begin, select one or more traffic
analysis zones corresponding to the
geography of your

6
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.460
project.

7
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.100
Then, choose one or more strategies to
model.

8
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.940
Find relevant strategies by filtering
based on category, tag, or keyword.

9
00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.700
We'll begin by configuring the
employer-provided commute benefits.

10
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.820
Let's assume that each transit trip costs
$3 and that 50% of area employers
participate

11
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.100
in the program.

12
00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:02.180
Next, we'll configure the workplace
parking pricing.

13
00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:11.820
Let's assume that workplace pricing
increases to $12 per day.

14
00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.780
After adding to the cart, click View
Results to be taken to the results screen
to see the

15
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.820
impact of these strategies.

16
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:26.740
You can download a CSV with full
calculations and underlying data, or
export a PDF to share.

17
00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.060
For more details, see the attached user
guide.
